    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a high-ceiling matchup today, anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 74.56 score makes him our clear offensive focal point. Facing Nick Martinez (4.63 xERA), **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable dynamic platoon split (+14%) and the premium production expected from the #3 hole (+6%). **Kyle Tucker** also warrants attention; despite being slotted in the #8 spot, his base projection holds strong, resulting in a 61.22 score. While the drop-off in batting order penalizes his raw output, his ability to provide reliable production in a neutral-to-favorable matchup against Mahle keeps him firmly in the \"Strong\" start category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Liam Hicks**, who sat just below our 40.0 \"Below Floor\" threshold at 38.61. While the park factors were favorable (+4%), his platoon disadvantage against the southpaw Fried ultimately forced the optimizer to bench him in favor of protecting our daily game caps. Meanwhile, we are forced to navigate a difficult slate for **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci**; both are battling elite SP skill from Espino (2.51 xERA), which heavily suppresses their scores. **Miguel Vargas** in particular remains a marginal play at 40.49, as the drag from an elite catcher\u2019s pop time offsets his solid xwOBA.\n\nLooking ahead, we remain cautious regarding the deployment of **Jackson Merrill**. His 54.01 score is buoyed by his speed profile\u2014specifically a +2% boost for favorable stolen base conditions against Gasser\u2014but he faces a significant -13% penalty due to platoon constraints against the left-handed starter. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** currently unavailable due to off-days or injury, the margin for error is thin. We are monitoring the lineups for **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara** to ensure we aren't leaving production on the table against these difficult pitching matchups. **Drake Baldwin**, **Brayan Rocchio**, and **Andy Pages** round out the active group, all operating in the 40\u201359 range, requiring disciplined management to ensure we maximize our utility without burning through remaining caps prematurely.",
